name duel-emcon-1
timeout 600

# THE ASYMMETRIC DUEL, GEOMETRY 5 OF 8: THE EMCON PROBE — the MiG-29 flown the way its own doctrine
# says it should be (doc/modules/mig29/datalink-gci.md), against the same F-16 as duel-headon.fbm.
#
# THE DUEL IS THE SAME HEAD-ON GEOMETRY. ONE THING CHANGES: the N019 EMISSION SWITCH STARTS ON OFF,
# and a ground controller calls the fighter loud at commit range instead of at t=0. That single switch
# moves three things at once, and only one of them is in the MiG's favour:
#
#   FOR   the F-16's ALR-56M has nothing to hear. In duel-headon its RWR lit up at t=17.4 s, six and a
#         half seconds BEFORE its own radar found anything — the MiG announced itself first.
#   FOR   the SPO-15's forward hemisphere is no longer blanked by its own transmitter
#         (sensors.md §5.6), so the MiG can finally HEAR the APG-68 that is working it. In duel-headon
#         its eng_threat_s is -1: it never knew it was being tracked, and never defended.
#   AGAINST  a silent N019 is a blind N019. This aircraft's pilot flies on radar contacts alone; the
#         KOLS is powered here and its contacts reach the bus, but pilot/FBPilot's intercept picture is
#         built from the RADAR block (doc/duels.md, gap D3), so until ILLUM the MiG has only the
#         controller's four numbers.
#
# The APG-68 sees a 4.0 m^2 target at ~100 km whatever the MiG transmits, so EMCON buys NO delay in
# being FOUND. What it buys is the warning and the surprise, and this mission measures whether that is
# worth the blindness it costs.
#
# THE CONTROLLER'S SCRIPT: one call at t=170 s, by which time the pair is inside 30 km. Three typed
# entries follow (scan elevation by the range-angle method, ZONE, then ILLUM), each charged its own
# DED latency, so the set radiates ~8 s after the call and needs a further ~6 s (two 3 s frames) to
# build its first contact.
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 (TIMEOUT), both alive — and the MiG survives an AIM-120 for the only time in
# the campaign. MEASURED, and every line of it is the switch:
#   t=0.1    the MiG's SPO-15 already has the APG-68, because nothing of its own is blanking the
#            forward hemisphere. In duel-headon its eng_threat_s is -1 for the whole run: it never
#            knew it was being worked, and never defended.
#   t=16.9   NOTHING appears on the F-16's ALR-56M. In duel-headon it had the MiG at t=16.9, 7.1 s
#            before its own radar found anything.
#   t=140.8  missile-launch warning; the MiG answers 1.1 s later and beams for 118.9 s.
#   t=173.2  the AIM-120 arrives 8.29 m out instead of the 7.52 m of duel-headon — and the beam is why
#            it is not closer. 50.5 kJ/m^2 in the NOSE zone: air data, radar altimeter, nav, radar,
#            fire control and datalink all fail; engine, flight controls and structure do not.
#            `dmg_effective` stays 1.
#   t=174.2  the controller's commit call arrives INTO that. The ILLUM entry is refused
#            (`sequence_precondition` — the manoeuvre lock, this jet is pulling), the pilot retries at
#            t=176.3 as any other briefed entry is retried, and THAT one is refused
#            `system_failed`: the box it was meant for no longer exists.
# So EMCON bought the MiG the warning, the defence and its life, and cost it the engagement: it never
# radiated, never detected, never fired. That trade is the doctrine, measured in one run.

unit viper
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 6.40000 8000 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set store 8 aim9
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 46.90000 8.40000 8000 450
  objective kill unit fulcrum
  objective survive

unit fulcrum
  team hostile
  module mig29
  spawn 46.90000 7.85000 8000 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_range_nm 27
  set n019_emission off                     # SILENT: the whole point of the mission
  set kols_mode ir                          # the passive alternative, powered and publishing
  set kols_laser on                         # ...and armed, so a contact inside 6 km gets a range
  set rwr on
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r27r
  set store 5 r73
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set brief_gci 170 270 28 8                # "bandit bearing 270 for 28, angels 8" — commit, go loud
  set task intercept
  wp 46.90000 5.85000 8000 450
  objective kill unit viper
  objective survive
